***************************** T A L Y S **************************4125 1451  188
                                                                  4125 1451  189
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   4125 1451  190
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      4125 1451  191
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    4125 1451  192
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     4125 1451  193
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  4125 1451  194
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        4125 1451  195
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    4125 1451  196
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         4125 1451  197
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      4125 1451  198
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    4125 1451  199
stored in this data file:                                         4125 1451  200
                                                                  4125 1451  201
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   4125 1451  202
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     4125 1451  203
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 4125 1451  204
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   4125 1451  205
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                4125 1451  206
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   4125 1451  207
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    4125 1451  208
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        4125 1451  209
- Recoil data                                                     4125 1451  210
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           4125 1451  211
- Total particle energy spectra                                   4125 1451  212
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      4125 1451  213
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        4125 1451  214
- Residual production cross sections                              4125 1451  215
                                                                  4125 1451  216
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            4125 1451  217
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        4125 1451  218
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   4125 1451  219
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                4125 1451  220
                                                                  4125 1451  221
